~ start
do fade_to_black(0.5)
???: No.
???: I don't care that he signed off on these numbers, they're wrong.
do show_cg("julian_intro", "none", 0.0)
# step 2.396: Julian's intro theme, for the CG only: it rises with the fade from black and fades with the
# fade to black below
do SoundManager.play_music_track("julian_intro_theme", 1.5)
do fade_from_black(0.8)
???: Then he can call me himself.
Player: Oh.
Layla: You know him?
Player: That's Julian. He's usually not in this early.
Player: I can't stand his guts.
Layla: Is he a grad student like you, Fiona? 
Player: Yes, he works in Dr. Ember's lab. Biochem. Our rivals.
Layla: Oh.
Julian: ...I'll call you back.
Julian: Fiona.
Player: Julian.
Julian: What's this? Your department's recruiting new blood already?
Julian: That's optimistic.
Player: This is Layla. And yeah, she actually-
Layla: Just visiting.
Player: (???)
Julian: Hmm. Well, enjoy the tour.
Julian: It'll be a short one. Their department doesn't have much to show these days.
Player: Yeah, like yours does. 
Julian: Well, anyway... I've got work to get back to.
Player: Yeah. Us too. 
Player: (Jerk...)
do SoundManager.fade_out_music(1.5)
do fade_to_black(0.4)
do hide_cg("none", 0.0)
# step 2.375: the two of them stand face to face over the dimmed room (Fiona left, Layla right, flipped to
# face her, like the wake-up talk). they enter under the black and their slide-in settles before the fade
# lifts, so the CG cuts cleanly to the pair. Layla's expressions come from her rig.
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "wowed", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
do wait(0.5)
do fade_from_black(0.5)
Layla: That was intense!
do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
Layla: What's the deal between you two?
do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: Well, for us at the genomics lab, the biochem department poses a real threat.
Player: Since we compete for the same sources of funding.
do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
Layla: Oh... that's unfortunate.
do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Tell me about it.
# caught out (same pose)
do actor_change("Layla", "troubled")
Player: Anyway, why didn't you tell him you're the new Research Assistant for the Genomics lab?
do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
Layla: I don't know! He seemed so intimidating. 
do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
Layla: I thought he'd dismiss me if I told him I'm just an undergrad RA.
do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
What do you want to say to Layla?

- Everyone starts somewhere [matters]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_julian_intro_encouraged", true)
	do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", 1)
	do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back")
	Player: I'd suggest you not worry too much about it.
	Player: All of us start somewhere.
	do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
	Layla: Yeah... you're right.
	do actor_change("Layla", "admiring")
	Layla: Thanks, Fiona.
	do actor_change("Layla", "warm")
- Right [matters]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_julian_intro_agreed", true)
	do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", -0.5)
	do actor_change("Fiona", "shrug")
	Player: Yeah... an undergrad RA holds basically no standing amongst grad students.
	Player: He might've dismissed you indeed.
	do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
	Layla: Yeah...
	Layla: That's what I thought.
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
	do actor_change("Fiona", "hands_back_sad")
	Player: (... she's gone quiet.)

do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Right. Anyway, I don't like him much.
do actor_change("Fiona", "shy")
Player: He's good at his work though. Annoyingly.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_julian_intro_agreed") == false and Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
	Layla: Well if you don't like him, I don't like him.
do actor_change("Layla", "asking")
Layla: Also, who was he talking to like that? On the phone?
do actor_change("Layla", "attentive")
do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
Player: (I suppose he did say something about some wrong numbers getting signed off...)
Player: (Wonder what that was about.)
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: Don't know.
Player: Don't care.
Player: Anyway, let's get back to what we were doing.
do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
Layla: Right!

